  "id": "kursk_kuvikly",
  "name": "Kuvikly (Kursk women's panpipe playing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Women's playing of kuvikly (also kugikly), sets of two to five cane or reed pipes of graded length, in the villages of Kursk and Bryansk oblasts in southern Russia. Several players each hold a set and divide the tune between them, alternating blown notes with short sung whoops so that pipes and voices interlock; the practice was captured in Melodiya field recordings from Kursk villages and taken up by the Dmitri Pokrovsky Ensemble.",
  "recipe": "classic modern kuvikly, drone Modal, wind pipe branch, Slavic baltic domestic rhythm. single lead single track no stacking. kugikly. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
